{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And to his father he sent like these, etc.</b> The reason it says <b>ke-zot</b> and did not suffice with what is explicit is that since it says ״נשאים מטוב מצרים״ and it was not known what is the ״good of Egypt,״ therefore it prefaced by saying ״ke-zot״ — to say: of the kind mentioned in the adjacent passage, garments and silver vessels, of the choicest found of this kind in Egypt. And according to our Sages of blessed memory (Megillah 16b) who said ״the good of Egypt״ — aged wine; and according to the one who said (Genesis Rabbah 94:2) ground beans of fava, the verse would be deficient a vav, as though it said ״ka-zot va-asarah״ etc., and the intent in saying ״ke-zot״ is as we explained, plus ten etc." "<b>And ten, etc., to his father, etc.</b> The reason it repeated a second time to say <b>to his father</b> — it intends to say that he did not send them to him as part of the adjacent shipment, but rather he gave them to his brothers and told them that they are for his father, for the journey."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:58.137846550Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}